# PROJECT — Mozentai

## Mission

Corporate landing page for **Mozentai**, an engineering company (embedded engineers, auditing, hardening, CITC credentials). Static site at **https://mozentai.com**.

## Conventions

1. Never use emojis unless told otherwise.
2. For text, never use em dash, en dash, or double hyphens as separators. Use commas instead.
3. **All user-facing copy is English.** No Portuguese section titles or labels.
4. Minimize scope. Match existing Jekyll, CSS, and data-file patterns.
5. Learn from mistakes; when corrected, update `cortex.mdc` in this repo and mirror to `~/github/context/mozentai/rules/`.
6. Do not commit secrets, credentials, or `.env*` files.

## Deploy (mandatory)

**After any change that should go live, ALWAYS push and deploy at the end without being asked:**

1. `git status`, `git diff`, `git log` (parallel)
2. Stage relevant files, commit with a clear message
3. `git push origin main`
4. Watch deploy: `gh run watch $(gh run list --workflow=pages.yml --limit 1 --json databaseId --jq '.[0].databaseId')`
5. Confirm live URL: https://mozentai.com

Never skip deploy when site content or assets changed.

## Content rules

- **Hero:** full viewport, wordmark + tagline only. Do not clutter above the fold. MOZENT△I is sized to the viewport lockup, not shrunk to the tagline.
- **Below fold:** Pitch ("Stop wasting time on screening."), stats, Services (Auditing, Hardening, Engineering, CITC), Career Wall (lookup + Python Engineer I/II/III as exams P1/P2/P3), Clients marquee, Certifications, Get in touch CTA, footer Conway glider. No Leadership, no Testimonials, no How We Work cards. Keep the client companies.
- **Get in touch:** dedicated `/hire/` page, headline "Get in touch" (never "Hire a security engineer"). Form delivers to victor@mozentai.com and writes Firestore inquiries. Keep the hero wordmark-only.
- **CITC:** Council of Information Technology & Computing. We prepare professionals. Companies look them up and skip screening. Public page does not print prices, Stripe, SmartHex, CPF, CREA, or the five-title cap. Mechanics live in cortex.
- **Career Wall:** Registered engineers only. Site-color portraits. Lookup by name, CITC number, title, or exam. Cards show P1, P2, P3. Public copy may mention the questionnaire or scheduling with an instructor. Do not print HTB, PX, scores, or the question bank. Do not invent people.
- **Manager inbox:** `/login/` is unlisted. 404 until Victor signs in with Google from an IP in Firestore `config/allow.ips`. Do not link it from the public site.
- **Clients:** Axonius-style infinite horizontal logo marquee (EU, US, and Brazil logos).
- **404:** dedicated `error` layout, message "Got lost on the way home?"
- **Logos:** PNG only in `assets/clients/`. Never ship SVG client logos. Use official artwork for real clients (SANEARES PNG).

## What belongs here

- Jekyll layouts, includes, `_data/` YAML, SVG assets, GitHub Pages workflow

## What does not belong here

- Backend services, secrets, customer PII, production app code
